From f0daaea498965292e3b66d295090180c803f464e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:26:59 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: add AVS2 decoding

The video engine of the Allwinner H616 (and of other SoCs of its
generation) decodes AVS2 (GB/T 33475.2, IEEE 1857.4) Main and Main10
in the H.265 engine slot, selected with bits 31:30 of register 0x04.
Software parses the sequence and picture headers; the engine is started
at the first slice start code and decodes all the slices of the picture
in one run.

The engine reads the adaptive loop filter coefficients, the weighting
quantization matrices and the reference picture list from a 512 byte
buffer in memory. Each entry of the reference list holds the addresses
and the picture order count of a reference, and the picture order counts
of its own references, for the temporal motion vector prediction from
the co-located picture (the first reference). The co-located motion
vectors are stored in a buffer per capture buffer, 128 bytes per 64x64
block.

The register sequence and the layout of the table buffer were recovered,
for interoperability, from the debug information and the disassembly of
the vendor libawavs2.so (libcedarc); no vendor code is used.

10-bit pictures use the low-2-bit plane and P010 output of the H.265 and
VP9 decoders. The VE is reset when it is switched to or from AVS2, as
for VP9. Field coded sequences are rejected for now.

The decoder is not enabled on any variant yet.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
